MobileGlues: the ASTC encoder with no vector indexed by a variable and no array arguments.

A Pixel 10's PowerVR crashed compiling it on Android 16 (Pocket Foundry #65), as it was and with only its vectors by
name; without the array arguments it compiles. b[w] and e0[k][c] are now each component by name (astc_or,
astc_try's channels), and the arrays astc_weights, astc_try and astc_ise took are globals. On Mesa's llvmpipe it
makes the same blocks, bit for bit, on 4,096 of each BC kind.

